#: source/how-to/run_deformable_object.rst:198
msgid ""
"To run the same tutorial with the experimental Newton deformable backend:"
msgstr "使用实验性 Newton 可变形后端运行同一教程："

#: source/how-to/run_deformable_object.rst:216
msgid ""
"This should open a stage with a ground plane, lights, and several cubes. Two"
" of the four cubes must be dropping from a height and settling on to the "
"ground. Meanwhile the other two cubes must be moving along the z-axis. You "
"should see a marker showing the kinematic target position for the nodes at "
"the bottom-left corner of the cubes. To stop the simulation, you can either "
"close the window, or press ``Ctrl+C`` in the terminal"
msgstr ""
"这应打开一个包含地面、灯光和若干立方体的舞台。四个立方体中，两个从高处落下并停在地面，另外两个沿 z "
"轴运动。立方体左下角的节点应显示运动学目标位置标记。关闭窗口或在终端按 ``Ctrl+C`` 可停止仿真。"

#: source/how-to/run_deformable_object.rst:221
msgid "result of run_deformable_object.py"
msgstr "run_deformable_object.py 的结果"

#: source/how-to/run_deformable_object.rst:226
msgid ""
"This tutorial showed how to spawn deformable objects and wrap them in a "
":class:`DeformableObject` class to initialize their physics handles which "
"allows setting and obtaining their state. We also saw how to apply kinematic"
" commands to the deformable object to move the mesh nodes in a controlled "
"manner. The ``deformables`` example provides a more advanced example, "
"including surface deformables, loading USD assets, and applying deformable "
"materials."
msgstr ""
"本教程展示了如何生成可变形物体，并用 :class:`DeformableObject` "
"类封装它们、初始化物理句柄，从而设置和读取状态。还展示了如何施加运动学命令，以受控方式移动网格节点。 ``deformables`` "
"示例提供了更进阶的用法，包括表面可变形物体、加载 USD 资产和应用可变形材料。"
